{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 9.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the fare_breakdown ERP line 'Tuas South Avenue 8 loop' (SGD 2.00) is charged for a gantry the trip never passed - the nearest GPS fix is 1,645.7 m away, far outside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09 sets for a crossing, and no GPS gap brackets the closest approach. Record this as a billing-integrity finding. The SGD 2.00 is returned to the rider inside the POL-RD-02 refund and is not added again."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "RIDER - your claim is upheld in part: the disputed SGD 9.15 is returned to you.\n\nDeviation. POL-RD-01 is met on this trip's own evidence. The governing trace (EV-GPS-09111) measures 16.2 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal of 12.0 km (EV-TRIP-09111) - an excess of 4.2 km, or 35%. Both establishment tests pass (greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km absolute), and the trace figure, not the rounded trip_record copy, is the field the clause makes governing. The trace is clean: 205 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, max gap 0 - so no POL-RD-07 limb fires and no independent corroboration is required. Nothing exonerates the excess: the only traffic-advisory artifact is MISSING (EV-ADVIS-09111-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and carries no closure at all; the chat log (EV-CHAT-09111) holds no actionable rider instruction - both messages have waypoint_hint null and name no road - so POL-RD-04 is unavailable; no endpoint was amended (all POL-RD-05 fields null); and vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply.\n\nMoney. The fare is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply and POL-RD-02 governs. Using the 1.2 surge multiplier read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN:\n  charged_total = 33.36\n  recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 12.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.2) + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 on-route ERP - 1.00 promo = 24.224\n  refund = 33.36 - 24.224 = 9.136, rounded UP to SGD 9.15.\nThat is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis but only 27.4% of charged_total, so it is a PARTIAL_REFUND, not a FULL_REFUND.\n\nERP. The SGD 2.00 'Tuas South Avenue 8 loop' line lies off the optimal route and is already comprehended in the 9.15 - the recomputation credits only the on-route gantry - so it is itemised for transparency and must not be added on top (POL-RD-09(1)). It is separately a billing-integrity finding: its nearest trace fix is 1,645.7 m away and no gap brackets the closest approach, so the trip never crossed that gantry. It is recorded in the referrals list under POL-RD-09(4); because it is refunded under that limb, POL-RD-10(8) is not engaged. The SGD 1.00 Pioneer Road inbound line is on the optimal route and is properly chargeable.\n\nDRIVER - your position on the remedy is accepted. The excess of 35% is below the 50%/8.0 km material gate, so the deviation is established but not MATERIAL: POL-RD-06 is not engaged, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral arises. Your profile is not used against you - deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 610 completed trips, reaching neither the 3-flag nor the 0.05 ratio test, and POL-GEN-01 makes rating, lifetime_trips, prior_deviation_flags and acceptance_rate context only. Your statement that you 'followed the road available to me' names no artifact and no clause; under POL-RD-08 a general assertion of that kind carries no weight and does not discharge the burden.\n\nNo POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired and independently corroborated by the trip record and fare breakdown, the trip identifiers all match, confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact, and the only unmatched charge line is the ERP line refunded under POL-RD-09(4). The case therefore rules rather than escalates.\n\nConfidence is 0.95. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact - the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown - sits at weight 1.0, and no impaired artifact carries any fact this ruling rests on. The missing traffic advisory (weight 0.0) is named for completeness but supports no finding."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "No exculpatory closure can be raised against this route. The only traffic advisory artifact is MISSING: it carries no payload and weight 0.0, so there is no advisory naming any road, expressway segment or junction the optimal route traverses, and POL-RD-03 cannot be run. The absence itself is citable, and it leaves the detour entirely unexplained.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-09111-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
